### The same flows as demo.sh, one request at a time.
### Works with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code (and similar tools that support
### named requests). Start the app first: docker compose up --build
###
### Demo accounts (password demo-pass): acme-admin, acme-operator, acme-employee,
### globex-admin, globex-operator, globex-employee. Demo only.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Health (no token needed)
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### 1. Log in as an operator
# @name loginOperator
POST {{host}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "acme-operator", "password": "demo-pass" }

###
@operator = {{loginOperator.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Log in as an admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "acme-admin", "password": "demo-pass" }

###
@admin = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3. Send a trip with a 22-minute GPS hole and a drop-off inside it
### (change "tripRef" in sample-trip.json to send it again as a new trip)
POST {{host}}/api/trips
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
Content-Type: application/json

< ./sample-trip.json

### 4. Read it back
GET {{host}}/api/trips/DEMO-1
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}

### 5. Why is every kilometre there? One line per segment, with the rule that priced it
GET {{host}}/api/trips/DEMO-1/segments
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}

### 6. Close the invoice (admin only; an estimated trip is refused with 409)
POST {{host}}/api/trips/DEMO-1/bill
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### 7. Late pings after billing: shows up as a signed adjustment, the invoice stays as it was
POST {{host}}/api/trips/DEMO-1/pings
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
Content-Type: application/json

< ./late-pings.json

### 8. The adjustments (admin only)
GET {{host}}/api/trips/DEMO-1/adjustments
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### 9. FAILURE DEMO: switch the routing provider off
POST {{host}}/api/admin/routing/outage
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "down": true }

### 10. Send a trip that needs routing: it comes back DEGRADED (estimate), and billing it gives 409
POST {{host}}/api/trips
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
Content-Type: application/json

< ./sample-trip-outage.json

### 11. Provider back
POST {{host}}/api/admin/routing/outage
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "down": false }

### 12. Recompute (the background job would also do this within 30 seconds)
POST {{host}}/api/trips/DEMO-2/recompute
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}

### 13. Another tenant cannot see it: 404, same as a trip that does not exist
# @name loginOther
POST {{host}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "globex-operator", "password": "demo-pass" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/trips/DEMO-1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOther.response.body.accessToken}}

### 14. Metrics (admin only)
GET {{host}}/actuator/prometheus
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
